Here we want to make sure that ArrayList's Contains method behaves correctly when called. 

1. `PUT_ContainsContract` accepts an `ArrayList arrList` (ArrayList under test) and an `int x` (the item to test for existance in `arrList`). 
2. We keep track of the list's count before and after the operation, as well as the index of `x` in the list before and after the operation.
3. We then execute `arrList.Contains(x)` and get the count and index information again.

