- ArrayListContractTest: The contract test class seems to be correct and does not show any flaws. However, the tests are only for the ArrayList class but the contract should also be applied to other classes too according to the principle of property testing. Flaws will be apparent when we apply property-testing principles on methods of other classes too. So, this class is a successful one at this stage.

- ArrayListTest: The flawed contract in ArrayListTest class can be attributed to lack of proper testing of ArrayList's methods. The contract needs to be designed and tested for all methods in the ArrayList class to ensure its correctness.

